WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.920
Gather around, sci-fi fans - YouTube wants
to tell you an Origin story.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.700
If you're confused about how the first season
of the big-budget YouTube Premium show wrapped

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.799
up, and what the developments may mean for
the show to come, keep watching as we break

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.100
down the twist-filled ending of the streaming
service's newest hit.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.600
Origin starts on board a spaceship of the
same name with a small group of people left

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.780
behind, one hour after an unexplained evacuation.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.430
Each passenger is seeking a new start, with
a clean slate promised by the mysterious SIREN

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.550
organization, and their colonization project
on the distant planet Thea.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.260
It's a framework that justifies a lot of distrust
between the passengers, especially the first

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.510
two we meet - former Yakuza member Shun, and
former bodyguard Lana.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.570
Their relationship is founded on skepticism,
but the two have little choice but to work

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.060
together.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.260
Despite mutual paranoia, they become the leaders
of the surviving passengers.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.030
The end of the season focuses on their relationship,
with the two forming a tentative trust…

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.300
that ends in brutal betrayal.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.340
The alien thing
When the passengers come across injured crew

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.559
members Evelyn Rey and Dr. Max Taylor, they
soon discover that Taylor's possessed by an

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.160
alien parasite, trying to mimic the behavior
of a normal human being.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.760
"Who are you?"

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:17.180
"Max Taylor… medic… human."

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.180
An autopsy reveals the alien to be a slender
worm that installs itself in the brain, where

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.820
it can survive and reproduce.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.100
While the one attached to Taylor dies, one
more lives on, taking up residence in the

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.250
head of a crewman who calls himself Eric - which
Lee later discovers is not his real name.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.760
After Fake Eric is discovered to be another
alien host, the passenger Henri makes an attempt

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.300
to blast him out an airlock.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.920
The plan fails, but Eric is still defeated
shortly after.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.740
When his brain is examined, it's found that
the alien escaped.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.640
Thus begins a season-long mystery - which
one of the passengers did the surviving alien

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.140
jump to?

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.240
As Origin draws nearer to Thea with the mystery

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.249
of the alien still unresolved, the ship's
AI goes into a fail-safe mode, activating

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:01.780
a security plan called Protocol 47.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.770
Detecting the presence of an alien life form,
the ship begins emitting a lethal gas, moving

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.819
through the ship with the aim of killing everything
on board.

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:13.739
Suddenly, instead of simply waiting out the
threat, the survivors are forced to either

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.840
solve the mystery, or die trying.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.640
With Origin barrelling toward Thea with no

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.020
easy answers in sight, the passengers stockpile
oxygen tanks to try and wait things out.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.319
But then Shun makes a horrifying discovery.

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:30.319
Separate from the other passengers, he comes
across two vital pieces of information: a

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:35.040
video diary of Max reciting a childhood memory
that Lana later presented as her own, and

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.080
an audio recording of "Lana" rehearsing her
own humanity.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.000
"They know I'm still here…

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.840
I'm the only one still here"
As it turns out, the alien never had anything

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.239
to do with the suspicious Baum or Katie.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.240
The truth is indisputable: Lana is the alien.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.180
But when did she become infected?

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.500
In the beginning, Lana really is who she says

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.500
she is.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.220
But halfway through the season, she ends up
with the parasite that originally existed

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.330
in Fake Eric.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.630
To fill in the blanks, the final episode goes
back to a few critical moments, showing new

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.439
perspectives of what really happened while
most of the characters weren't looking.

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:16.010
When Fake Eric escaped from Henri's attempted
airlock attack at the end of episode four,

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:18.810
he fled to a pool room, finding Lana.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.670
Hunted, injured, and desperate to survive,
the alien attacked her, travelling between

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.530
the two of them and killing the first host
in the process.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:30.549
This means that our heroine turned evil offscreen
sometime between episodes four and five.

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:34.489
Ever since then, we've been watching a Lana
working to deceive the others, and keep its

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:36.060
alien self alive.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.030
After taking over Lana, the alien sabotaged
any equipment that might have helped test

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.140
for its presence.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.549
It also killed Lee, and framed Katie.

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:48.370
It's only found out because of its one known
weakness - it can't access people's memories.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.640
But in Lana's case at least, this doesn't
seem so clear-cut.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.139
Lana seems to still be in there somewhere
- not just bringing up old memories, but actually

00:03:56.139 --> 00:03:58.170
fighting for control of her own body.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:02.159
With that info in mind, it doesn't sound like
the Lana we knew will be gone for long.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.400
If the series gets a second season, you can
bet our heroine will figure out a way to vacuum

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.400
out that alien worm.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.200
Before all of this happens, Rey and Abigail

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.740
make a discovery that's arguably even more
chilling than their encounters with the aliens.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.260
Not only are there terrifying monsters in
this system that mimic human beings, SIREN

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.810
seemed to know about them.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:25.260
Specifically, Rey and Abigail discover that
Thea has a neighboring world, Iris , that

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.670
was kept secret from both passengers and crew.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:32.460
Based on video footage and files they find,
it seems like it may be the alien homeworld

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.060
- and it's very dangerous for humans.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:39.560
Rey deduces that SIREN knew the planet was
populated by hostile aliens, and sent the

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.680
Origin ship toward Thea anyway.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.531
The company also prepared for possible close
encounters without telling most of the people

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.040
on board.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:53.380
"That's why protocol 47 exists — bc SIREN
knew there was hostile life near Thea."

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:59.020
Protocol 47, as Rey points out, is an emergency
measure designed specifically to annihilate

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.960
crews compromised by parasites.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.190
But the show also hints at the secret in more
subtle ways.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.660
In the third episode Rey flashback, Dr. Taylor
is surprised to discover that the ship has

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.420
guns onboard.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.730
Also, Captain Sanchez seems extremely certain
that Cell 50 is a lost cause when it's breached

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:19.260
by an asteroid impact - almost as though she
knew that asteroid might carry hostile life.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.970
It's information that throws everything the
crew and passengers may have took on faith

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:23.980
into serious doubt.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.440
With that in mind, it's hard to imagine what
might be waiting on the planet's surface.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.770
Paradise as promised?

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.200
Or some terrible new threat?

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.580
The season ends with an ominous message, and

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:37.670
it couldn't be more clear of a warning - "Don't
land on Thea."

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:41.940
Given what the Origin passengers know by the
final episode, all the lofty promises they've

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.590
been sold about Thea become questionable at
best.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.210
Iris, at least, seems completely overrun by
the same aliens the Origin passengers have

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:50.540
been evading for a week.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.960
Is Thea compromised too?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.760
Origin doesn't end in a way that wraps things
up conclusively.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.770
It feels like it's just getting started.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:01.660
What is SIREN's real goal on Thea, and why
don't the passengers know about it?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.420
What's the situation on the planet?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.830
Will Henri survive?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:05.850
What about Lana?

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:10.810
And hey, is that conversation about faster-than-light
experiments, spacetime curves and time travel

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.030
going to amount to anything?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:19.200
"they're like tiny time travel machines or your future."

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:24.320
One way or another, it seems the Origin survivors
are far from done fighting for their lives.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.400
Maybe they should just turn the ship around,
and try returning to Earth.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:27.900
Who knows?

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.440
The possibilities seem endless, so here's
hoping we get to see what all these Origin

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.389
stories are building toward with a season
two.

